1
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,679
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:07,699 --> 00:00:10,979
Basil hangs his bar magnet on a string, so it can turn

3
00:00:10,999 --> 00:00:11,749
freely.

4
00:00:12,029 --> 00:00:13,779
He spins it again and again.

5
00:00:14,059 --> 00:00:15,239
Where does it stop?

6
00:00:15,294 --> 00:00:17,354
One, a different way every time.

7
00:00:18,564 --> 00:00:20,634
Two, the same way every time.

8
00:00:22,110 --> 00:00:23,620
Hold on to your answer!

9
00:00:26,092 --> 00:00:29,712
Today, we find out where a hanging magnet stops, and why!

10
00:00:30,209 --> 00:00:32,599
A little swallow is hiding in this video.

11
00:00:32,849 --> 00:00:34,089
Can you spot it?

12
00:00:34,212 --> 00:00:37,552
Swallows swoop low over a field, catching tiny insects.

13
00:00:37,742 --> 00:00:39,152
Look high, and look low!

14
00:00:39,199 --> 00:00:40,659
You against the Buddies!

15
00:00:40,929 --> 00:00:42,779
Lock in first with your fingers.

16
00:00:43,049 --> 00:00:44,879
One finger for every point.

17
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:46,760
Today you'll learn:

18
00:00:46,964 --> 00:00:48,974
A freely suspended magnet.

19
00:00:49,170 --> 00:00:50,850
The North-South direction.

20
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:52,740
Earth is like a magnet.

21
00:00:53,238 --> 00:00:54,178
Are you ready?

22
00:00:54,618 --> 00:00:55,388
Three!

23
00:00:55,768 --> 00:00:56,428
Two!

24
00:00:56,798 --> 00:00:57,448
One!

25
00:00:57,868 --> 00:00:58,588
Go!

26
00:00:59,977 --> 00:01:00,867
Round one!

27
00:01:01,167 --> 00:01:03,057
Where does Basil's magnet stop?

28
00:01:03,337 --> 00:01:04,647
Show me your fingers!

29
00:01:08,118 --> 00:01:09,098
Locked in!

30
00:01:09,226 --> 00:01:09,946
One!

31
00:01:10,096 --> 00:01:13,136
My spinning top falls over a different way every time.

32
00:01:13,236 --> 00:01:14,666
So will the magnet!

33
00:01:14,719 --> 00:01:15,599
Two.

34
00:01:15,829 --> 00:01:17,519
Magnets follow rules.

35
00:01:17,729 --> 00:01:20,489
Unlike poles attract every single time.

36
00:01:20,543 --> 00:01:21,173
Two!

37
00:01:21,333 --> 00:01:22,503
I tried it at home.

38
00:01:22,633 --> 00:01:25,803
The red end always stopped facing my bedroom window!

39
00:01:26,077 --> 00:01:27,537
Be the hanging magnet!

40
00:01:27,817 --> 00:01:28,807
Shrink down.

41
00:01:29,087 --> 00:01:30,017
Quietly.

42
00:01:32,304 --> 00:01:34,914
You are a bar magnet, hanging on a string.

43
00:01:35,714 --> 00:01:38,374
A giant finger spins you round and round!

44
00:01:38,899 --> 00:01:39,969
Slower now.

45
00:01:40,739 --> 00:01:43,139
You swing past a line, and back again.

46
00:01:43,909 --> 00:01:46,589
Something you cannot see turns you gently back.

47
00:01:47,113 --> 00:01:50,493
You stop, with your red end facing the big rain tree.

48
00:01:51,273 --> 00:01:52,453
A spin again!

49
00:01:53,243 --> 00:01:54,653
Slower, and slower.

50
00:01:55,443 --> 00:01:56,403
You stop.

51
00:01:57,223 --> 00:01:58,693
The rain tree again!

52
00:02:00,344 --> 00:02:03,194
The answer is two: the same way every time!

53
00:02:03,454 --> 00:02:05,034
Did you show two fingers?

54
00:02:05,274 --> 00:02:06,673
Put one finger up!

55
00:02:06,693 --> 00:02:09,803
Every time, it comes to rest with its red end facing the

56
00:02:09,823 --> 00:02:10,743
rain tree.

57
00:02:11,033 --> 00:02:13,143
Let's mark the line with two cones!

58
00:02:13,264 --> 00:02:14,774
I think I know why.

59
00:02:14,904 --> 00:02:17,244
The red end faces the goalpost.

60
00:02:17,414 --> 00:02:20,624
Magnets attract steel, so the goalpost turns it.

61
00:02:21,274 --> 00:02:22,424
Look closer.

62
00:02:23,024 --> 00:02:26,470
Hang it in the middle of the field, far from the goalpost.

63
00:02:26,490 --> 00:02:28,030
Hang it in the classroom.

64
00:02:28,610 --> 00:02:31,813
Float it on a plastic lid in a basin of water.

65
00:02:31,833 --> 00:02:35,113
Every time, it comes to rest along the same line.

66
00:02:35,683 --> 00:02:37,668
This line runs North and South.

67
00:02:37,688 --> 00:02:41,358
Freely suspended means hanging so that it can turn freely, such as

68
00:02:41,378 --> 00:02:42,988
a magnet on a string!

69
00:02:43,496 --> 00:02:47,266
The North-South direction means the line from North to South, such as

70
00:02:47,286 --> 00:02:49,216
the line between our cones.

71
00:02:49,546 --> 00:02:52,716
One end faces North, and the other end faces South.

72
00:02:56,020 --> 00:02:57,180
Say it with me!

73
00:02:57,888 --> 00:03:01,998
A freely suspended magnet comes to rest in the North-South direction.

74
00:03:04,625 --> 00:03:05,515
My turn!

75
00:03:05,615 --> 00:03:08,795
My string got tangled, so I laid the magnet on the bench.

76
00:03:09,015 --> 00:03:11,085
Nobody is holding it, so it is free!

77
00:03:11,225 --> 00:03:13,545
But it stops a different way every time.

78
00:03:13,669 --> 00:03:15,229
Something is not right.

79
00:03:15,499 --> 00:03:17,679
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

80
00:03:17,959 --> 00:03:18,919
Hold on!

81
00:03:24,332 --> 00:03:25,462
Arms crossed?

82
00:03:25,732 --> 00:03:26,942
One finger up!

83
00:03:26,994 --> 00:03:27,864
Watch.

84
00:03:28,054 --> 00:03:30,974
The bench rubs on the magnet and stops it turning.

85
00:03:31,254 --> 00:03:33,694
I hang it up, and it turns freely again!

86
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:36,888
A freely suspended magnet must be free to turn.

87
00:03:36,908 --> 00:03:37,548
Oops!

88
00:03:37,698 --> 00:03:40,168
Free to turn, not just free from my paws.

89
00:03:40,368 --> 00:03:42,898
But how does the magnet know which way is North?

90
00:03:42,968 --> 00:03:44,555
Nothing is touching it!

91
00:03:44,575 --> 00:03:48,065
Maybe a giant magnet is hiding somewhere, turning it round!

92
00:03:48,715 --> 00:03:49,845
Look closer.

93
00:03:50,445 --> 00:03:54,338
Fly up, above Singapore, until you can see the whole Earth.

94
00:03:54,358 --> 00:03:58,478
All over the world, freely suspended magnets come to rest in the

95
00:03:58,498 --> 00:03:59,951
North-South direction.

96
00:03:59,971 --> 00:04:01,621
Basil is nearly right.

97
00:04:02,201 --> 00:04:07,241
Earth behaves like a magnet, with its own North and South poles.

98
00:04:07,766 --> 00:04:11,386
So the Earth turns my magnet round, without even touching it!

99
00:04:14,082 --> 00:04:15,302
Say it with me!

100
00:04:16,016 --> 00:04:19,806
Earth behaves like a magnet with its own North and South poles.

101
00:04:20,436 --> 00:04:23,266
It interacts with a freely suspended magnet.

102
00:04:23,856 --> 00:04:27,986
This causes the freely suspended magnet to always point in the North-South

103
00:04:28,006 --> 00:04:28,916
direction.

104
00:04:31,389 --> 00:04:32,849
Show me your score hand!

105
00:04:33,129 --> 00:04:34,159
Two fingers?

106
00:04:34,439 --> 00:04:35,809
You beat the Buddies.

107
00:04:36,089 --> 00:04:37,089
High five!

108
00:04:37,667 --> 00:04:39,097
Did you spot the swallow?

109
00:04:39,387 --> 00:04:41,397
It was on the rim of the netball hoop!

110
00:04:41,522 --> 00:04:42,832
Here is a fun fact!

111
00:04:42,892 --> 00:04:46,022
Every year, swallows fly to Singapore from far away.

112
00:04:46,282 --> 00:04:49,442
Many birds can feel the Earth's magnet, and it helps them find

113
00:04:49,462 --> 00:04:50,322
their way!

114
00:04:50,444 --> 00:04:51,724
Tell someone at home!

115
00:04:52,453 --> 00:04:54,653
Let's read today's key words together!

116
00:04:54,943 --> 00:04:55,703
Ready?

117
00:04:55,990 --> 00:04:57,360
Freely suspended.

118
00:04:59,154 --> 00:05:00,625
North-South direction.

119
00:05:02,559 --> 00:05:04,329
Earth behaves like a magnet.

120
00:05:06,581 --> 00:05:07,521
Well done!

121
00:05:08,318 --> 00:05:08,928
Look!

122
00:05:09,178 --> 00:05:12,418
My compass needle lines up with Basil's cones too.

123
00:05:12,518 --> 00:05:14,217
Is the needle a magnet?

124
00:05:14,237 --> 00:05:15,827
Find out in Part Two!

125
00:05:16,987 --> 00:05:18,088
Say it with us!

126
00:05:18,888 --> 00:05:19,638
Ready?

127
00:05:19,761 --> 00:05:20,421
One!

128
00:05:20,761 --> 00:05:21,461
two!

129
00:05:21,766 --> 00:05:22,941
Now you know!
